<title>KYRGYZSTAN: Kazakhs to send Kyrgyzstan one mln T oil in 1997.</title>
<headline>Kazakhs to send Kyrgyzstan one mln T oil in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BISHKEK 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan will provide the neighbouring Central Asian state of Kyrgyzstan with one million tonnes of oil in 1997, a Kyrgyz foreign ministry official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The official, who said the deal was agreed during Kyrgyz President Askar Akayev's official visit to Kazakhstan last week, said the oil would be refined at the former Soviet republic's Chui and Dzhalal Abad oil refineries.</p>
<p>-- Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
